+## Check configured effort levels
+
+Use the effort configurator's read-only check mode to verify the lane efforts used by a
+benchmark run. Pass `--check` with one or more `--expect lane=value` arguments and the
+same `--settings-file` used for the run:
+
+```sh
+python3 plugins/astral-orchestrator/scripts/configure-effort.py \
+  --settings-file /path/to/effort-levels.toml \
+  --check \
+  --expect orchestrator=high \
+  --expect luna=xhigh \
+  --expect terra=xhigh \
+  --expect reviewer=high
+```
+
+Check mode always prints a JSON report. It includes the effective `effort` settings,
+requested `expectations`, `matched`, and per-lane `mismatches`; `changed` is always
+`false`. It exits zero only when every expectation matches, and non-zero for a mismatch
+or invalid check request. It only reads the supplied settings file and never creates,
+writes, or otherwise changes it.
+
